    "title": "pandas.api.typing.SeriesGroupBy.cumcount — pandas 3.1.0.dev0 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.api.typing.SeriesGroupBy.cumcount#\n\n- \nSeriesGroupBy.cumcount(*ascending=True* )[source]#\n- Number each item in each group from 0 to the length of that group - 1. Essentially this is equivalent to self.apply(lambda x: pd.Series(np.arange(len(x)), x.index)) \n  - Parameters:\n    - **ascending** bool, default True\n    - If False, number in reverse, from length of group - 1 to 0.\n  - Returns:\n    - Series\n    - Sequence number of each element within each group.\n See also \n  - `ngroup`\n  - Number the groups themselves.\n Examples >>> df = pd.DataFrame([[\"a\"], [\"a\"], [\"a\"], [\"b\"], [\"b\"], [\"a\"]], columns=[\"A\"]) >>> df A 0 a 1 a 2 a 3 b 4 b 5 a >>> df.groupby(\"A\").cumcount() 0 0 1 1 2 2 3 0 4 1 5 3 dtype: int64 >>> df.groupby(\"A\").cumcount(ascending=False) 0 3 1 2 2 1 3 1 4 0 5 0 dtype: int64",
    "markdown_length": 803,
